    "body": "## What changed\n\n- add production `Game.Telemetry` schema v1 with anonymous/session/page-view identity, ordered events, foreground dwell, visibility, abandonment/return, screen/modal/action/choice/state/question/cycle instrumentation\n- persist a bounded 30-day local queue and provide export/readback/summary APIs\n- keep network transmission disabled by default; require explicit consent, same-origin HTTPS, credential omission, 50-event batching, offline persistence, bounded retry, and concurrent-flush deduplication\n- instrument Stage 7 decisions/questions/cycles, shared stable-ID clicks, the essence modal, and real argument-battle choices\n- preserve byte-identical source/docs mirrors and document the privacy/transport contract\n\n## Privacy\n\nNo player-authored text, input values, DOM snapshots, profile fields, secrets, URLs, query strings, or hashes are collected. Free-form string values that are not valid stable IDs are discarded.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 tools/test_behavioral_telemetry.py`\n- `node tools/test_behavioral_telemetry_runtime.mjs`\n- Stage 7 observed-evidence, rendered-runtime, cosmetic, essence, personalization, payoff, aftermath, DM, and toast lifecycle checks\n- production-equivalent Chromium smoke: modal open/close, main-screen detection, session persistence across reload, persisted session_end, transport disabled, zero non-GET requests\n- source/docs parity and `git diff --check`\n\nFour legacy Stage 7 tests remain red on both this branch and clean `origin/main` because their expected copy/cache markers are stale; they are not regressions from this change.",
